From a3dcc8a8ac2d7189fdf2d5669fd1bc1569ad6e5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:32:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SECURITY: bound the OIDC discovery fetch at ten seconds

/auth/oidc fetched {issuer}/.well-known/openid-configuration with no
timeout of its own, so a provider that accepted the connection and said
nothing held the request open for as long as the socket lived, and each
retry held another. Discovery now aborts after ten seconds (the price
providers' default), body included, and the give-up is an OAuthError,
which the route already answers 503 without recording a server fault.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
